====== Rosewill RNX-N150RT ======
This is a [[..:TP-Link:tl-wr741nd|TL-WR741ND v1]] but will only accept firmware with a Rosewill vendor byte in the file header. OpenWRT currently does not have the byte by default. DD-WRT has everything we need, so we can use it to bootstrap. (As an alternative, you could try the [[toh/rosewill/rnx-n300rt#automatically_edited_header_method|script made for the RNX-N300RT]] to add the missing byte to the correct firmware file for this router. At the time of writing, the script method is untested for this model. Please add your experience to this wiki page if you try it.)

===== Debricking =====

Serial Connector Soldering is the only way to recover, be careful! THERE IS NO WAY TO TFTP OVER ETHERNET.

===== Convert Rosewill RNX-N150RT to a TP-Link TL-WR741NDv1 using DD-WRT =====
  - Flash dd-wrt: ftp://ftp.dd-wrt.com/others/eko/BrainSlayer-V24-preSP2/2012/07-20-12-r19519/rosewill-rnx-n150rt/factory-to-ddwrt.bin this image has Rosewill RNX-N150RT vendor bytes which OpenWRT currently lacks.
  - Download //tl-wr741nd_v1_v2-webrevert.bin// from http://www.dd-wrt.com/phpBB2/viewtopic.php?p=521071#521071 **You must be logged in to see it**. __**Be sure that you unrar the file!**__. The SHA1 checksum of "tl-wr741nd_v1_v2-webrevert.bin" (inside the .rar) is 537d38fc644d905ba0b6f37038d58884952175a6. You can find the file on another website and verify that the checksum matches.
  - Flash "tl-wr741nd_v1_v2-webrevert.bin". This converts your router to a **TP-Link**.
  - Flash **OpenWRT** version 12.09-rc1 or later: http://downloads.openwrt.org/attitude_adjustment/12.09-rc1/ar71xx/generic/openwrt-ar71xx-generic-tl-wr741nd-v1-squashfs-factory.bin . (-factory firmware NOT -sysupgrade)

